{
  "style": "Soft paper-craft diorama rendering meets Monument Valley's serene geometry and Royal Match's glossy premium polish. Everything reads as layered cut paper and matte clay: rounded chunky shapes, no hard black outlines, only gentle tonal edge shifts and a thin lighter rim-light on the top-left edge. Light is warm late-afternoon from the upper left, with soft ambient occlusion and feathered contact shadows (low-opacity indigo, never black) that give 2-4 px of stacked-paper depth. Map is a pastel top-down tabletop of rolling paper hills, rivers and parks with subtle paper grain and faint vignette; transit lines are thick, rounded, slightly satin ribbons with a soft highlight stripe and gentle drop shadow. Stations are cream enamel discs with slate rims and bold paper glyph tokens. Colour is harmonious and low-stress: dusty teal, sage, warm cream, apricot and lavender, with saturated line colours kept clean and distinct. Warnings glow in feathered yellow to amber halos, never red, never hard-edged. Mood: cosy, unhurried, tactile, like a bedtime toy train set. Shiny gold accents and soft bloom are reserved for rewards and heritage stations.",
